Help Type: command
Command: {{ commandName }} <uri> {{ predicate }}

URI Predicate Command

Target:
  {{ displayUri }}

Predicate:
  {{ predicate }}

{% if predicate == "related" %}
Purpose:
  Expand from the current chunk or entity object to nearby objects.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} related [--query <query>] [--skip-unindexed] [--reverse] [--all] [--limit <n>] [--context <n>] [--cursor <token>] [--role <any|subject|object|self>] [--evidence [n]] [--json|--jsonl]

Notes:
  - Chunk targets return nearby Reading Graph chunks.
  - Entity targets return Knowledge Graph triples involving the entity.
  - `--query` filters and ranks related results with the current search index.
  - Add `--skip-unindexed` only with `--query` when you intentionally want to search indexed chapters and ignore uncovered chapters.
  - Without `--query`, `--reverse` reads Document Flow order backward. See `{{ commandName }} help uri`.
  - `--role` only applies to entity targets.
  - Use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} evidence --help` when source grounding is the main goal.
{% elif predicate == "evidence" %}
Purpose:
  Trace the current object back to source-backed evidence.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} evidence [--query <query>] [--skip-unindexed] [--reverse] [--all] [--limit <n>] [--context <n>] [--json|--jsonl]

Notes:
  - Evidence is for grounding, verification, and citation support.
  - `--query` filters and ranks evidence with the current search index.
  - Add `--skip-unindexed` only with `--query` when you intentionally want to search indexed chapters and ignore uncovered chapters.
  - Without `--query`, `--reverse` reads Document Flow order backward. See `{{ commandName }} help uri`.
  - Evidence previews include nearby source context by default; use `--context 0` for exact cited ranges.
  - To trace an evidence passage to an imported PDF or EPUB location, move its sentence fragment to `<chapter-uri>/source/locators#<range>`; read `{{ commandName }} help source-locators`.
  - Source and scope URIs are not evidence targets.
{% elif predicate == "pack" %}
Purpose:
  Build bounded Agent-readable context around the current chunk or entity object.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} pack [--budget <chars>] [--json|--jsonl]

Notes:
  - Default budget is 5000 characters.
  - Use this after selecting a useful chunk or entity.
  - Use `evidence` first when verification matters more than context assembly.
{% elif predicate == "create" %}
Purpose:
  Create the archive at this URI.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} create [--import <source-file>] [--replace] [--json]

Notes:
  - Without `--import`, create an empty `.wikg` archive.
  - `--import <source-file>` creates the archive and imports the source file's metadata, structure, and source text.
  - File import also records source provenance so normalized source text can be traced back to the imported file.
  - The imported file itself is not embedded in the `.wikg` archive.
  - `create` does not read stdin. Read `{{ commandName }} help file-import` for supported source files and import boundaries.
  - File import runs only the import/source stage and does not call an LLM provider.
  - Existing archives are not overwritten by default. Use `--replace` only when the target archive should be discarded and recreated.
  - Parent directories must already exist.
  - On success, text output is the archive object (`<archive>`). With `--json`, output is `{"uri":"..."}`.

Examples:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} create --json
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} create --import ./book.epub

Next:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} inspect
{% elif predicate == "export" %}
Purpose:
  Export a projection from this archive.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} export [--output-format markdown|txt|epub] [--output <path>]

Notes:
  - Default output format is markdown when omitted by the parser, but explicit `--output-format` is recommended.
  - Without `--output`, exported content is written to stdout.
  - `--json` and `--jsonl` are not supported; the output stream is the exported projection.
  - Text exports depend on available source/summary content. Missing summaries produce an error that points to the generation command.
  - Export does not build Reading Graph or Knowledge Graph coverage.
  - Projections are portable views; they do not replace the `.wikg` archive.

Examples:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} export --output-format markdown --output book.md
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} export --output-format txt > book.txt
{% elif predicate == "inspect" %}
Purpose:
  Inspect archive readiness before `--query`, retrieval, or starting generated work.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} inspect [--json]

Notes:
  - Run this before broad Reading Graph, Reading Summary, or Knowledge Graph work.
  - The report includes content counts, search index readiness, generation coverage, retrieval guidance, recommended next commands, planning estimates, and concurrency hints.
  - Use `--json` for a machine-readable report with the same recommendations.
{% if libraryContext.isArchiveShortcut %}
  - This library archive shortcut inspects one managed archive's readiness; it is not a library-level health report.
{% endif %}
{% elif predicate == "build" and target.name == "chapter-index-artifact" %}
Purpose:
  Queue a job to build or replace this chapter index artifact.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} build [--json]

Notes:
  - This command enqueues work; it does not wait for the artifact to be built.
  - A queued response means the artifact is not ready yet. Use the returned job id with `{{ commandName }} wikg://local/job/<job-id> watch` to follow progress.
{% if "/index/fts" in uri %}
  - FTS artifacts are local compilation work and do not call a provider.
{% else %}
  - Source and summary embedding artifacts require `wikg://local/config/embeddings` and may call the configured provider.
  - Building an embedding artifact can immediately enqueue or run provider-backed work and may incur provider cost.
{% endif %}
  - Direct artifact build is an explicit build request; it does not use `--accept-cost`.
{% if "/index/embedding/summary" in uri %}
  - Summary embedding artifacts require an existing non-empty chapter summary.
{% endif %}
  - After artifacts change, sync the archive or library index cache before library query; archive-level query can create a missing archive cache from current artifacts on first use.
{% elif predicate == "add" and target.name == "chapter-collection-scope" %}
Purpose:
  Add a chapter to the archive.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} add [--parent <chapter-uri>] [--title <title>] [--input <path|->] [--json]

Notes:
  - Without `--input`, creates an empty planned chapter placeholder.
  - With `--input <path|->`, reads non-empty UTF-8 plain text, does not infer a
    format from the file name, and creates the chapter in the `source` stage.
  - This plain-text path does not create a source-text map or call an LLM
    provider. Read `{{ commandName }} help file-import` for source locators.
  - Chapter handles are opaque and are not derived from `--title`; reuse the
    returned `locatedUri` for later commands.

Output:
  - Text output includes `Chapter`, the archive-relative handle, and `Located URI`, the complete target for later commands.
  - With `--json`, the same values are `uri` and `locatedUri`; reuse `locatedUri` for later commands.
{% elif predicate == "add" and target.name == "job-collection-scope" %}
Purpose:
  Add a local build job.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} add --input <archive-uri|chapter-uri> --task index-fts|index-embedding-source|index-embedding-summary|reading-graph|reading-summary|knowledge-graph [--accept-cost] [--depth <N>] [--boost] [--llm <json>] [--prompt <text>]

Notes:
  - `index-fts` builds chapter FTS artifacts locally and does not require `--accept-cost`.
  - `index-embedding-source` and `index-embedding-summary` build Dense artifacts with `wikg://local/config/embeddings` and require `--accept-cost`.
  - Reading Graph, Reading Summary, and Knowledge Graph jobs may call an LLM provider and require `--accept-cost`.
  - Reading Graph and Knowledge Graph jobs require a current FTS artifact for the chapter.
  - Summary embedding jobs require an existing non-empty summary.
  - Archive input adds jobs for all eligible chapters; chapter input expands to the chapter subtree by default.
  - For archive-wide indexing, use `{{ commandName }} wikg://local/job --json` to inspect the jobs and re-run archive `inspect` to verify coverage.
  - Use `--depth <N>` with archive or chapter input to limit affected chapters. For archive input, depth is measured from the archive's root chapters; for chapter input, it is measured from the specified chapter. `--depth 0` means only the relevant root chapters or specified chapter.
  - `--llm <json>` stores a job-local LLM object; it does not update `wikg://local/config/llm`.
{% elif predicate == "move" %}
Purpose:
  Move this chapter in the chapter tree.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} move --parent <chapter-uri> [--first|--last] [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} move --root [--first|--last] [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} move --before <chapter-uri> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} move --after <chapter-uri> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} move --first [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} move --last [--json]

Notes:
  - Moves only the chapter tree node. Source text, Reading Graph data, and summary stay attached to the same internal chapter record.
  - `--parent <chapter-uri>` moves the chapter under another chapter.
  - `--root` moves the chapter to the top level.
  - `--before <chapter-uri>` or `--after <chapter-uri>` moves the chapter next to the target chapter.
  - `--first` or `--last` moves within the target parent when combined with `--parent` or `--root`.
  - Without `--parent` or `--root`, `--first` and `--last` reorder within the current parent.
  - Cannot move a chapter into or next to its own descendant.
{% elif predicate == "remove" %}
Purpose:
  Remove this chapter.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} remove [--recursive] [--json]

Notes:
  - Removes the target chapter from the TOC tree.
  - Removes that chapter's source text, Reading Graph data, and summary.
  - Fails when the chapter has children unless `--recursive` is provided.
  - With `--recursive`, removes the whole selected subtree and its stored data.
  - This is a destructive in-place edit. Read the chapter tree first when the archive is important.
{% elif predicate == "reset" %}
Purpose:
  Delete later-stage artifacts for this chapter.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} reset --to planned|source|reading-graph [--json]

Notes:
  - `planned` deletes source text and provenance, Reading Graph, Knowledge Graph,
    summary, and all chapter index artifacts.
  - `source` keeps source text and provenance, and deletes Reading Graph,
    Knowledge Graph, summary, and all chapter index artifacts.
  - `reading-graph` keeps source text and provenance, Reading Graph, Knowledge
    Graph, and the source embedding artifact. It deletes summary, FTS, and the
    summary embedding artifact.
  - `reading-summary` and `knowledge-graph` are not supported reset targets.
  - Reset is destructive and may discard generated work.
{% elif predicate == "set" %}
{% if target.name == "chapter-tree-object" %}
Purpose:
  Replace the chapter tree with a JSON tree document.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --input <tree.json|->

Notes:
  - The input is a chapter tree JSON document produced by the chapter tree view.
  - Use `--input -` to read the tree JSON from stdin.
  - This rewires chapter hierarchy and order; it does not rewrite chapter source text or generated graph content.
{% elif target.name == "chapter-source-object" %}
{% include "help/commands/shared/chapter-source-set.jinja" %}
{% elif target.name == "chapter-summary-object" %}
Purpose:
  Replace this chapter summary text.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set [text] [--input <path|->]

Notes:
  - The input is plain summary text from a positional value, `--input <path>`, or `--input -` for stdin.
  - This sets the summary resource directly; it does not call an LLM provider.
{% elif target.name == "chapter-title-object" %}
Purpose:
  Replace this chapter title.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set <title>

Notes:
  - Use `clear` on the same title URI to remove an explicit title.
{% elif target.name == "job-target-object" %}
Purpose:
  Change the generation target for this local job.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set reading-graph|reading-summary|knowledge-graph

Notes:
  - This changes what the job will generate when resumed or picked up by a worker.
  - Use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} --help` to inspect the current job target first.
{% elif target.name == "metadata-object" %}
Purpose:
  Replace this metadata map with a JSON object.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set <json> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --input <path|-> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --json-input <json> [--json]

Notes:
  - Metadata shape depends on whether this is archive metadata or object metadata.
  - `--json-input <json>` reads an inline JSON object.
  - `--input <path|->` reads a JSON object from a file or stdin.
  - `--json` controls output shape; it is not JSON input.
  - `put`, `delete`, and `clear` are usually safer for single-key metadata edits.
{% elif target.name == "local-config-section" %}
Purpose:
  Replace this entire local config section with a JSON object.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set <json> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --json-input <json> [--json]

{% if "/llm" in uri %}
Schema:
  {
    "provider": "openai|openai-compatible|anthropic|google",
    "model": "<model-name>",
    "baseURL": "<url>",
    "name": "<display-name>"
  }

Notes:
  - Allowed keys: provider, model, baseURL, name, apiKey.
  - `apiKey` is sensitive and cannot be set from JSON.
  - If current output shows `"apiKey":"****"`, passing the same masked value preserves the existing secret.
  - To add or replace the secret, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put apiKey --secret`.
  - To remove the secret, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete apiKey`.
{% elif "/embeddings" in uri %}
Schema:
  {
    "provider": "openai|openai-compatible",
    "model": "<embedding-model-name>",
    "baseURL": "<url>",
    "name": "<display-name>",
    "dimensions": 1536
  }

Notes:
  - Allowed keys: provider, model, baseURL, name, dimensions, apiKey.
  - `apiKey` is sensitive and cannot be set from JSON.
  - If current output shows `"apiKey":"****"`, passing the same masked value preserves the existing secret.
  - To add or replace the secret, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put apiKey --secret`.
  - To remove the secret, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete apiKey`.
  - `dimensions` must be a positive integer and is sent only to providers/models that support dimension control.
{% elif "/wikispine" in uri %}
Schema:
  {
    "provider": "fetch|cli",
    "endpoint": "<optional-service-base-url>"
  }

Notes:
  - Allowed keys: provider, endpoint, token.
  - `fetch` uses the hosted WikiSpine endpoint by default and requires its Bearer API key.
  - `cli` runs the local `wikispine` command from PATH.
  - `token` is sensitive and cannot be set from JSON.
  - To add or replace it, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put token --secret`.
  - To remove it, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete token`.
{% elif "/wikimedia" in uri %}
Schema:
  {
    "endpoint": "<optional-service-base-url>"
  }

Notes:
  - Allowed keys: endpoint, token.
  - An empty section uses direct local Wikimedia access. Setting `token` enables the hosted resolver; `endpoint` is optional.
  - Remote access requires `token`; `endpoint` alone is incomplete.
  - `pnpm dev` defaults to `https://pdf-craft-api.oomol.dev`; built CLI artifacts default to `https://api.pdfcraft.ai`.
  - `token` is sensitive and cannot be set from JSON.
  - To add or replace it, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put token --secret`.
  - To remove it, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete token`.
{% elif "/job" in uri %}
Schema:
  {
    "endpoint": "<service-base-url>"
  }

Notes:
  - Allowed keys: endpoint, token.
  - `token` is optional and sensitive; it cannot be set from JSON.
  - To add or replace it, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put token --secret`.
  - To remove it, use `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete token`.
{% elif "/concurrent" in uri %}
Schema:
  {
    "job": 3,
    "request": 6
  }

Notes:
  - Allowed keys: job, request.
  - Values must be positive integers.
{% endif %}

Examples:
{% if "/llm" in uri %}
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"provider":"openai","model":"gpt-4.1"}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --json-input '{"provider":"openai-compatible","model":"model-name"}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"provider":"google","model":"gemini-2.5-pro"}' --json
{% elif "/embeddings" in uri %}
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"provider":"openai","model":"text-embedding-3-small"}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --json-input '{"provider":"openai-compatible","model":"embedding-model","baseURL":"https://api.example.com/v1"}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put dimensions 1536
{% elif "/wikispine" in uri %}
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"provider":"fetch"}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"provider":"cli"}'
{% elif "/job" in uri or "/wikimedia" in uri %}
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"endpoint":"https://service.example.com"}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put token --secret
{% elif "/concurrent" in uri %}
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set '{"job":3,"request":6}'
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} set --json-input '{"job":2,"request":4}'
{% endif %}
{% else %}
Purpose:
  This URI target has no generic `set` behavior.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} --help

Notes:
  - `set` is target-specific. Use the URI help page to find the writable child resource or supported predicate.
{% endif %}
{% elif predicate == "clear" %}
{% if target.name == "chapter-title-object" %}
Purpose:
  Remove this chapter's explicit title.
{% elif target.name == "metadata-object" %}
Purpose:
  Clear this metadata map.
{% else %}
Purpose:
  Clear this writable resource or local config section.
{% endif %}

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} clear{% if target.name == "metadata-object" %} [--json]{% endif %}

{% if target.name == "chapter-title-object" %}
Notes:
  - Removes the explicit title for this chapter.
  - This does not delete the chapter, source text, Reading Graph data, or summary.
{% elif target.name == "metadata-object" %}
Notes:
  - Clears all metadata keys for this metadata object.
  - No confirmation prompt is shown.
  - This does not delete the archive object or generated graph data.
{% elif target.name == "local-config-section" %}
Notes:
  - Clears every key in this local config section, including secrets.
  - No confirmation prompt is shown.
  - Success output is the now-empty JSON object: `{}`.
{% else %}
Notes:
  - This predicate is only available on URI targets that explicitly support clearing.
{% endif %}
{% elif predicate == "sync" and target.name == "index-object" %}
{% if libraryContext.isLibraryWide %}
Purpose:
  Sync this library index cache from registered archives' chapter index artifacts.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} sync [--jsonl]

Notes:
  - This is a cache rebuild from artifacts already stored inside member `.wikg` archives.
  - It does not build missing chapter artifacts and does not call an embeddings provider.
  - Missing or unreadable library archive members are skipped and reported.
  - Progress is emitted as text by default, or line-delimited events with `--jsonl`.
  - `--json` is not supported for sync because progress is streamed.
  - Library indexes are local derived state under Wiki Graph staging, not files inside the library folder.
  - Sync holds the library write lock; concurrent `arc scan`, `arc add`, `path set`, `clean`, archive `path set`, or archive `remove` commands for the same library cannot run at the same time.
  - Library query requires a current library index cache.
{% else %}
Purpose:
  Sync this archive index cache from chapter index artifacts.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} sync [--jsonl] [--skip-unindexed]

Notes:
  - This initializes or repairs the local `index.db` cache outside the `.wikg` archive.
  - It reads chapter index artifacts from the archive and does not call an embeddings provider.
  - If required chapter artifacts are missing, sync reports that artifact readiness problem instead of building them.
  - Add `--skip-unindexed` only when you intentionally want the cache to include indexed chapters and ignore uncovered chapters.
  - Archive-level query can create a missing cache from current artifacts on first use, but explicit sync avoids the first-query delay.
  - If query reports a missing or outdated cache, run this sync command before retrying.
  - With `--jsonl`, progress is emitted as line-delimited event records.
{% endif %}
{% elif predicate == "clean" and target.name == "index-object" %}
Purpose:
  Delete this index cache.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} clean [--json]

Notes:
  - This removes local `index.db` cache data only.
  - It does not delete chapter index artifacts, Knowledge Graph, Reading Graph, Summary, source text, or library membership.
  - Archive query can recreate an archive cache from artifacts when the selected scope supports lazy cache creation.
{% elif predicate == "clean" %}
Purpose:
  Remove completed local generation jobs.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} clean

Notes:
  - Removes succeeded, failed, and canceled jobs whose status has not changed for at least seven days.
  - Deletes those job records plus their workspace, cache, log, and event files.
  - Does not remove waiting, running, paused, or recently finished jobs.
  - Does not stop workers or cancel active jobs.
  - Does not support `--json`, `--jsonl`, `--dry-run`, or `--confirm`; output is a short text count.
  - Use `{{ commandName }} gc --help` for broader runtime cleanup and dry-run support.
{% elif predicate == "watch" %}
Purpose:
  Follow durable local job progress.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} watch [--jsonl] [--from beginning|now]
{% elif predicate == "pause" %}
Purpose:
  Pause this local job.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} pause
{% elif predicate == "resume" %}
Purpose:
  Resume this local job.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} resume

Notes:
  - Paused jobs move back to queued.
  - Queued jobs are already resumable work; `resume` leaves them queued and asks the local worker to pick up the queue.
  - Finished, failed, canceled, and canceling jobs cannot be resumed.
{% elif predicate == "cancel" %}
Purpose:
  Cancel this local job.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} cancel
{% elif predicate == "boost" %}
Purpose:
  Move this local job forward in the local job scheduler.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} boost
{% elif predicate == "put" %}
{% if target.name == "metadata-object" %}
Purpose:
  Set one metadata key.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put <key> <value> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put <key> --json-input <json> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put <key> --input <path|-> [--json]

Notes:
  - Positional `<value>` is stored as a string.
  - `--json-input <json>` stores a JSON value.
  - `--input <path|->` reads a value from a file or stdin.
  - `--json` controls output shape; it is not JSON input.
  - Metadata keys are command arguments, not URI segments.
{% else %}
Purpose:
  Set one key in this local config section.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put <key> <value> [--json]
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put <key> --json-input <json> [--json]
{% if "/llm" in uri %}
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} put <key> --secret [--json]
{% endif %}

{% if target.name == "local-config-section" %}
{% if "/llm" in uri %}
Keys:
  - provider: openai, openai-compatible, anthropic, or google
  - model: non-empty model name
  - baseURL: non-empty provider base URL string
  - name: non-empty display name
  - apiKey: secret; use `--secret`
{% elif "/embeddings" in uri %}
Keys:
  - provider: openai or openai-compatible
  - model: non-empty embedding model name
  - baseURL: non-empty provider base URL string
  - name: non-empty display name
  - dimensions: positive integer; numeric strings are normalized to numbers
  - apiKey: secret; use `--secret`
{% elif "/wikispine" in uri %}
Keys:
  - provider: fetch or cli
{% elif "/concurrent" in uri %}
Keys:
  - job: positive integer
  - request: positive integer
{% endif %}

Notes:
  - Positional `<value>` is stored as a string.
  - `--json-input` stores a JSON value and is useful for numeric config sections.
  - `--json` controls output shape; it is not JSON input.
{% if "/llm" in uri or "/embeddings" in uri %}
  - `--secret` reads the value from an interactive terminal without echoing it; use it for `apiKey`.
{% endif %}
  - Success output is the full section JSON with sensitive values masked.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% elif predicate == "delete" %}
{% if target.name == "chapter-index-artifact" %}
Purpose:
  Delete this chapter index artifact.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete [--json]

Notes:
  - This deletes the stored artifact from the `.wikg` archive.
  - It does not clean external `index.db` cache by itself; sync or clean the archive/library index cache after deleting artifacts.
{% elif target.name == "metadata-object" %}
Purpose:
  Delete one metadata key.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete <key> [--json]

Notes:
  - Deletes the key if present; deleting an absent key leaves the metadata map unchanged.
  - Metadata keys are command arguments, not URI segments.
{% else %}
Purpose:
  Delete one key from this local config section.

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} delete <key>

{% if target.name == "local-config-section" %}
Notes:
  - Deletes the key if present; deleting an absent key leaves the section unchanged.
  - Success output is the full section JSON after deletion.
  - Key aliases are normalized where supported, for example `api-key` to `apiKey`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% elif predicate == "test" %}
{% if "/concurrent" in uri %}
Purpose:
  Validate this local concurrency config section.
{% else %}
Purpose:
  Test connectivity for this local config section.
{% endif %}

Usage:
  {{ commandName }} {{ uri }} test [--json]

Notes:
{% if "/concurrent" in uri %}
  - Validates that configured `job` and `request` limits are positive integers.
  - This does not contact an external service.
{% else %}
  - For `llm`, this sends a small request to the configured model.
  - For `embeddings`, this sends a small embedding request and reports the returned vector dimensions.
  - For `wikispine`, this checks the built-in fetch service or local `wikispine` command.
{% endif %}
  - Text success output is intentionally short.
  - With `--json`, success and failure both return `{ "ok": true|false, ... }`; failures set a non-zero exit code.
  - Without `--json`, failures print the command error. Use `{{ commandName }} help readiness` and `{{ commandName }} help config` to recover.
{% if "/wikispine" in uri %}
  - Runtime setup and recovery guide: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oomol-lab/wiki-graph/refs/heads/main/docs/wikispine-runtime.md
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if libraryContext.isLibraryUri %}
Library context:
